    "text": "The Basilica di San Pietro in Vincoli, also known as Saint Peter in Chains, is a Roman Catholic titular church and minor basilica in Rome that houses the relic of the chains that bound Saint Peter and Michelangelo's famous statue of Moses. It is significant for its religious relics, Renaissance art, and architectural history.",
